Working principles for copy editors
In their work, copyeditors should be encouraged to observe certain principles. They should:

make essential changes only — if authors write correctly, their own wording should be kept;
make the manuscript easy to read and correct;
comment constructively when comment is needed;
look for answers from reference sources or previous issues of the journal before putting queries to an author;
keep queries to the author short and to the point.



Copyediting procedures
One possible method of working is to deal with all the required levels of editing together, during one or two readings of a manuscript, followed by a separate stage for cross-checking and styling references. Another method is to edit the language first, at the same time as substantive editing if this is required, followed by format and mechanical style, again with reference checking as a separate stage.

Running Head

Odd Pages
```{latex}
\shorttitle{CJILS/RCSIB Vol. 47, No. 2 (2024). DOI: 10.5206/cjils-rcsib.v-i--.--}

```


Even Pages
```{latex}
\leftheader{Lastname and Lastname}

```

Sections
\section{level 1 heading}
\subsection{level 2 heading}
\subsubsection{level 3 heading}
\subsubsubsection{level 4 heading}

Quotes
Quotes can go straight in the text when less than 40 words or three lines, otherwise use a long quote.
\begin{quote}
  This is a quote 
\end{quote}

Hyperlinks
use the \url{}
\url{https://www.somewebsite.ca/}

Single Column Table
\begin{table}
  \begin{tabular}
  \end{tabular}
\end{table}


Two-Column Table
\begin{table*}
  \begin{tabularx}
  \end{tabularx}
\end{table*}


Long Tables

Two column
\begin{table*}
  \begin{longtable}
  \end{longtable}
\end{table*}

Caption
The caption is the first element in the table.
\caption{\label{tbl-mytable}\textit{title of the table goes here}}

Linebreak after caption
Add \tabularnewline before you start adding rows to the table. Like this.

  &gt;{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{1.5in} 
  &gt;{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{2.5in}
  &gt;{\raggedleft\arraybackslash}p{2.5in} 
}
\tabularnewline

Putting it all together
\begin{table}
  \caption{Distribution of CJILS publications by country}
  \label{test}
  \begin{tabular}{
    &gt;{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{5.25cm}
    &gt;{\raggedleft\arraybackslash}p{1cm}
    &gt;{\raggedleft\arraybackslash}p{1cm}
  }
  \\
  \toprule
  \multirow{2}[b]{*}[-1.75ex]{Country} & \multicolumn{2}{r}{Publication\textsuperscript{*}} \\
  \cline{2-3}
  \\[-1.75ex]
  & N & Pct. \\
  \midrule
  Canada & 20 & 80\% \\
  United States & 5 & 20\% \\
  \bottomrule
  \\[-1.75ex]
  \multicolumn{3}{l}{\textsuperscript{*}Only includes research articles.}
  \end{tabular}
\end{table}

Make sure newtx package is not loaded in the preamble



This package creates a conflict and your document will not text in foreign languages.



Arabic example
The following code needs to be added to the preamble.
\usepackage[bidi=default,english]{babel}
\babelprovide[import]{arabic}
\babelfont[arabic]{rm}{Amiri}
Then Arabic text can be added to the document like this:
\foreignlanguage{arabic}{(جائحة)}


Indigenous languages example

In the preamble
\usepackage{fontspec}
\newfontfamily\inuktitutfont{Noto Sans Canadian Aboriginal}


